  <div class="container">
    <div class="content-text">
<p><span style="text-transform: uppercase"><span style="letter-spacing: 2.4pt"><b>197 - Evil Tongue of the World Harms and Damages the Humility</b></span></span></p><p><span class="body-text">Know that the world's evil tongue harms and damages humility – through such speech, it becomes impossible for&nbsp;</span><span class="body-text"><i>tzadikim</i></span><span class="body-text">&nbsp;to be humble, as evil tongue damage separates humility from wisdom. This damages humility, making it impossible, and even if achieved, it lacks wisdom. It is known that humility without wisdom is worthless; it is not a virtue to display humility foolishly by bowing the head as if humble – that is invalid humility. True humility is accompanied by wisdom. Evil tongue creates separation between humility and wisdom, preventing true humility.</span></p><p><span class="body-text">This was Moses our master's virtue: the Torah praises his immense humility, unaffected even by evil tongue. As written (Numbers 12:1): &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>And they spoke etc. against Moses</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; – evil tongue existed, yet &quot;</span><span class="body-text"><b>and the man Moses was very humble</b></span><span class="body-text">&quot; (Numbers 12:3), for his humility was at such a high level that evil tongue did not harm it.</span></p><p><br/><br/></p> 
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

